<Layout title="About Milksy – Baby Tracker by Davor" description="Milksy is a calm iPhone baby tracker built around quick logging, a chronological timeline and shared activity between parents." structuredData={authorSchema}>
 <article class="article-body"><p class="eyebrow">About Milksy</p><h1>About Milksy</h1><p>Milksy is an iPhone baby tracker for recording breastfeeding, bottle feeds and diaper changes. It is built around a simple idea: logging should take less attention than the thing you’re logging.</p><h2>Open. Log. Carry on.</h2><p>Parents have enough to remember. Milksy keeps the essential details in one place: a feed’s time, a bottle’s amount, which side you nursed on, and the last diaper change.</p><p>The Today feed puts daily activity in chronological order. Trends help you look back at the records, and iCloud family sharing lets parents contribute to the same baby log.</p><h2>Calm by design</h2><p>The app uses native Apple controls, soft blue and lilac backgrounds, and selective glass surfaces. Quick actions stay close to the timeline. Sleep, pumping, and medication or vitamin logs are available through the same logging flow.</p><h2>A record, not a rulebook</h2><p>Milksy records what you enter. Its familiar feeding intervals come from recent logs, not a prediction of your baby’s needs. It does not provide medical advice.</p><h2 id="davor">Made by Davor</h2><p>I’m Davor, a full-stack software developer in Sweden. I build Milksy for iPhone and iPad, alongside web and other software projects. You can find my work at <a href="https://davor.se/">davor.se</a>.</p><p>This website describes the app I make. The comparison pages disclose that connection and link to the sources used. For app questions or feedback, contact <a href="mailto:davor@davor.se">davor@davor.se</a>.</p><p>Explore the <a href="/baby-feeding-tracker/">feeding tracker</a>, <a href="/diaper-tracker/">diaper log</a>, or <a href="/baby-tracker-for-couples/">shared tracking for parents</a>.</p><StoreLink badge/></article>
</Layout>
